			(property "Description" "JXTCONN CSIM-H137-7P-class nano-SIM push-push socket, 7 pads (5 ISO7816 SIM signal contacts VCC/RST/CLK/GND/IO + 2-pin mechanical card-detect switch CD1/CD2). NOT on stock KiCad libs -- authored Task 11. DISCLOSED ASSUMPTION: the manufacturer's own pin-numbered pinout diagram could not be retrieved (LCSC C42420236, JLCPCB, bsc-elec, gct.co fetches all failed/blocked during authoring -- see task-11-report.md) -- this pin assignment follows the standard commodity nano-SIM push-push convention (5 signal + 2-pin CD switch = 7 pads, matching the part's '7P' designation) and needs confirmation against the physical part/real datasheet before layout lock. CD1/CD2 assumed normally-closed/shorted when card ABSENT, matching this project's cross-vendor-verified 'grounded=absent' DET convention (verification.md Item 7)."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
