	(text "U30 ST4SIM-200M (MFF2/VFDFPN8) pin table verified against ST data brief DB4082 Rev5 Fig.12/Table 4 (fetched via\nweb.archive.org -- live st.com/mouser.com fetches were blocked/timed out during authoring, flagged in task-11-report.md).\nPowered from UIM2E_VDD (module-switched, via mux NO1), matching the ISOLATION/DOMAIN note -- NOT board +3V3. Decoupling =\n100nF+1uF on VCC (Fig.6, datasheet-mandated) -- adds the 1uF the brief's terser '100nF VDD bypass' guess omitted. R119=20k\nI/O pull-up to VCC (Fig.13 PCB integration rec., 'R1: 20k external pull-up recommended on I/O'). UIM2E_DET has NO physical\nconnection to U30 (eSIM has no card-detect pin) -- it is purely the mux's NO5 channel (net now a single-pin float by design,\nfix pass 2026-07-15: R118's 100k-to-+3V3 pull-up removed -- see Q39 note below and task-11-report.md 'Fix pass'), so the\nmodule reads 'present' (floating, per the Sierra PTS two-state DET convention) automatically whenever SIM_SEL routes to the\neSIM branch.\nNo ESD/22pF TVS on this branch: fully on-board, no exposed card-edge contacts (only the two physical nano-SIM sockets carry\ninsertion/ESD/EMI risk) -- disclosed lighter treatment per the task brief's own invitation to make this call."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 145 208.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "36d2eaf1-f85a-4714-b94d-f6748896246f")
	)
	(text "SIM2 = physical slot 2, wired to U29's NC side (UIM2S_* -- sheet-local nets, not module-facing directly). D28=TPD4S009 ESD +\n22pF/line + 100nF VDD bypass, same treatment as SIM1 (exposed card-edge contacts -- ESD/EMI risk on both physical sockets).\nNO board-side DET pull-up (fix pass, 2026-07-15) -- same PTS two-state rationale as UIM1_DET; SIM2.CD2 floats through the\nmux's NC5 channel onto UIM2S_DET/module UIM2_DET when this slot is selected."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 6 199.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "49c45038-8c73-44bb-8d1f-a70e46e16769")
	)
	(text "SIM1 direct to module UIM1_* (CN1 pins 36/30/32/34/66 per m2 sheet). D27=TPD4S009 ESD (4ch: RST/CLK/IO/DET) + 22pF/line +\n100nF VDD bypass. NO board-side DET pull-up (fix pass, 2026-07-15): CN1.66/UIM1_DET is a module-internal-pull-up two-state\npin per the Sierra PTS (grounded=absent, floating=present) -- an added 100k-to-+3V3 pull-up put an undocumented third voltage\non a likely-1.8V-domain pin and was removed; floating is the correct 'present' presentation, matching SIM1.CD2's own\nNC-switch behavior."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 6 186.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5af4d5db-521d-4af4-a925-7c0598c821bc")
	)
	(text "Task 11 -- dual SIM (SIM1/SIM2 physical nano-SIM sockets, ISO7816 5-wire) + eSIM (U30, ST4SIM-200M, on-board MFF2) slot-2\noverride mux (U29, TS3A27518E). SIM1 wired direct to module UIM1_*. UIM2_* (module) lands on U29's COM side; NC side\n(default, SIM_SEL pulled low) = physical SIM2 socket (UIM2S_*); NO side (SIM_SEL driven high) = eSIM branch (UIM2E_*). Refdes\ncontinue from the 325-component project state -- SIM1/SIM2 is a fresh prefix; U29/U30/D27/D28/Q39 replace the brief's stale\nU11/U12/D10/D11/Q8 placeholders, which collide with already-placed ethernet-sheet parts (see task-11-report.md)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 6 173 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8f7c4801-e647-4fef-86a8-fd21330292de")
	)
	(text "Q39 (2N7002) + R119 (100k gate pull-down, reinforces RP2040's own internal pull-down default -- GP13/UIM2_DET_CTL blank-MCU\ndefault = OFF, no override) -- CORRECTED FUNCTION vs the brief's literal wording. Brief Step-3: 'Q8 2N7002 ...\ngate=UIM2_DET_CTL to assert present when eSIM active'. An N-channel FET can only pull its drain TOWARD GND -- i.e. it can\nonly assert the verified 'grounded=absent' state (verification.md Item 7), never the 'floating/pulled-up=present' state,\nregardless of topology (mux-channel or wired-OR). Implementing the brief literally would silently invert the DET polarity\nItem 7 verified cross-vendor. What's actually built: Q39 drain sits on UIM2_DET (module-facing, post-mux, COM5) and gives\nfirmware an active-high FORCE-ABSENT override, independent of which mux branch is selected (e.g. useful for a clean SIM\nhot-swap/provisioning sequence signaling 'treat as removed' before SIM_SEL switches). The 'present when eSIM selected' half\nof the requirement is satisfied by the mux's own routing alone (NO5=UIM2E_DET floats when SIM_SEL selects the eSIM branch,\nper the Sierra PTS two-state DET convention) -- fix pass 2026-07-15 removed R118 (the former 100k pull-up on UIM2E_DET),\nwhich put an undocumented 3.3V third state on this pin; a genuine float is the correct 'present' presentation, and no active\ndrive is needed or physically possible in the 'present' direction from a single NFET regardless. Full reasoning in\ntask-11-report.md 'Fix pass'."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 145 234.35 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a72b448d-3f91-43fc-8faf-98e2be5d5c44")
	)
	(text "U29 TS3A27518E truth table (Table 8-1, EN=L): IN=L -> NCx<->COMx ON / NOx<->COMx OFF; IN=H -> NOx<->COMx ON / NCx<->COMx OFF.\nIN1/IN2 tied together onto SIM_SEL so both 3-channel banks move as one 6-channel 2:1 mux. VCC=+3V3 (module drives UIM2_VDD up\nto 3.0V typ; TS3A27518E requires VCC > max analog signal, abs-max VCC=4.6V, rec. op. 1.65-3.6V -- +3V3 clears both). VIH\nmin=1.2V (Sec.6.3) << RP2040 3.3V GPIO VOH, so SIM_SEL/EN drive cleanly from GP11 without level shifting.\nSEL POLARITY (disclosed correction vs brief): brief's Step-3 text assigned NO=physical/NC=eSIM with a '100k pulldown =\nphysical slot' pull; per Table 8-1, IN=L(pulldown default) selects the NC side, not NO -- so NC/NO were SWAPPED here\n(NC=UIM2S_*/physical, NO=UIM2E_*/eSIM) to make the pulldown-default actually equal 'physical slot' as required, rather than\nflipping the pull direction. 100k pulldown (not pull-up) matches the project's established RP2040-reset-state fact\n(mcu.kicad_sch fix-pass note: pads reset with internal pull-DOWN ~50-80k) -- reinforcing, not fighting, that default avoids\nthe resistive-divider indeterminate-logic-level bug already caught once on this project (LED_EN_CTL R84).\nCH6 HYGIENE (fix pass, 2026-07-15): channel 6 (NC6 pin22, NO6 pin16, COM6 pin12) is unused by this design (only 5 of 6\nchannels are wired: VDD/RST/CLK/IO/DET). NC6 and NO6 -- the two switch-side pins that would otherwise float -- are tied to\nGND. COM6 is left NC-flagged (no_connect), not grounded: no local copy of the TS3A27518E datasheet's unused-channel note (if\nany) was available to check during this pass -- grounding NC6/NO6 while leaving the common pin open is the conservative\ndefault per TI's general floating-analog-switch-pin guidance (an ungrounded switch throw is higher-impedance/lower-risk than\nan ungrounded common), disclosed rather than silently assumed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 145 173 0)
